(7618750, 1233827, 67145, '<td valign="top">lol .. i think she should take the face out of the vase and revert to her ''normal'' appearance as she has become quite distorted .. not that there''s anything wrong with that .. !! .. <br/>to the pic .. i really like the clean lines of the vase against the black background and how you have been able to insert the face .. the distortion adds to the appeal .. like she''s under water .. this is very clever ... and i''m very impressed .. as i would have no idea how to achieve something like this .. :)</td>', 'lol .. i think she should take the face out of the vase and revert to her ''normal'' appearance as she has become quite distorted .. not that there''s anything wrong with that .. !! .. to the pic .. i really like the clean lines of the vase against the black background and how you have been able to insert the face .. the distortion adds to the appeal .. like she''s under water .. this is very clever ... and i''m very impressed .. as i would have no idea how to achieve something like this .. :)', '2019-03-10 23:53:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(7618751, 1233834, 67145, '<td valign="top">we had two peacocks that wandered around here .. wild .. but quite friendly .. we live rural .. they would visit .. and poo around the place .. and my dog katee would love to frighten them .. once one flew up onto our roof .. when katee barked .. they just appeared a few months ago .. we all wondered where they might have come from . ... then a few weeks ago they disappeared .. <br/>the other day one was back at my place wandering around . and his mate was no-where to be seen .. i felt sad for the bird who had a friend before and now had none .. <br/>anyway . i''m liking the clean lines of the vase and the gorgeous peacock feathers .. the birds we had visiting were a bit unkempt and their feathers didnt look even half as good as the ones you have in your vase .. <br/>i like how you have positioned them .. they look a bit like eyes . :)</td>', 'we had two peacocks that wandered around here .. wild .. but quite friendly .. we live rural .. they would visit .. and poo around the place .. and my dog katee would love to frighten them .. once one flew up onto our roof .. when katee barked .. they just appeared a few months ago .. we all wondered where they might have come from . ... then a few weeks ago they disappeared .. the other day one was back at my place wandering around . and his mate was no-where to be seen .. i felt sad for the bird who had a friend before and now had none .. anyway . i''m liking the clean lines of the vase and the gorgeous peacock feathers .. the birds we had visiting were a bit unkempt and their feathers didnt look even half as good as the ones you have in your vase .. i like how you have positioned them .. they look a bit like eyes . :)', '2019-03-10 23:56:30.000000', NULL, 1),
